title: mf script
tags: [[CLI command]] [[Scripting the GUI]]
kind: reference
summary: Your scripts, in ~/.config/metafolder/scripts/, and the templates to start one from (default: list)

Where your scripts are, and how to start one. The scripts are files of the
configuration, in `~/.config/metafolder/scripts/` ([[The configuration repository]]);
this command needs no daemon.

```
mf script                      # the directory, its scripts, the templates
mf script new sort-folder      # copy a template there, to adapt it
```

There are two kinds of shipped scripts. The ''scripts'' run as they are: the GUI
offers them (<<key "script:run" "g s">>, [[Running shipped scripts]]). The
''templates'', in `scripts/templates/`, are examples to copy and rewrite — not
offered to run, since a template's rules are yours to write
([[Writing a GUI script]]). <<cmd "mf script new">> copies one among the scripts,
where it runs beside the helpers it uses (`lib/`, `gui-tag-classify.sh`), and the GUI
offers it at once.

The development scripts of the source tree (`scripts/dev/`) are not shipped
([[Shipped defaults in the source tree]]).
